<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<PermissionSet xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <description>Field access for the new Disposition dashboard fields (listing date, broker check-in, days on market).</description>
    <fieldPermissions>
        <editable>false</editable>
        <field>BOV_Submission__c.Broker_Display__c</field>
        <readable>true</readable>
    </fieldPermissions>
    <fieldPermissions>
        <editable>false</editable>
        <field>BOV_Submission__c.Property_Name__c</field>
        <readable>true</readable>
    </fieldPermissions>
    <fieldPermissions>
        <editable>false</editable>
        <field>BOV_Submission__c.Selected_Broker__c</field>
        <readable>true</readable>
    </fieldPermissions>
    <fieldPermissions>
        <editable>false</editable>
        <field>Disposition__c.Days_On_Market__c</field>
        <readable>true</readable>
    </fieldPermissions>
    <fieldPermissions>
        <editable>true</editable>
        <field>Disposition__c.Listing_Date__c</field>
        <readable>true</readable>
    </fieldPermissions>
    <fieldPermissions>
        <editable>true</editable>
        <field>Disposition__c.Next_Broker_Checkin__c</field>
        <readable>true</readable>
    </fieldPermissions>
    <!--
        AMENDED 2026-08-31, TRANCHE 1 ITEM 11. Property_Asset__c.Argus_Value__c editable true to
        FALSE. readable stays true. This is the ONLY true downgrade in item 11: the two disposition
        sets never granted any Argus or CoStar field at all, so their entries are new grants at
        read only, and this set is the one place where an existing edit grant is being withdrawn.
        Argus_Value__c is a valuation carried from an external model and read by 8 of the 13
        disposition reports; a hand edit here changes what those reports say with no audit trail.

        ⚠ DELIBERATELY NOT CHANGED IN THIS PASS: Property_Asset__c.Property_Type__c and
        Property_Asset__c.Sell_Readiness_Score__c are still editable=true below. Neither is an
        Argus or CoStar field, so neither is in item 11's scope. They are flagged for a future
        pass, not silently fixed here.

        ⚠ THIS SET STILL CARRIES NO objectPermissions AT ALL, and that is reported rather than
        fixed. Its field grants are inert unless the running user gets Property_Asset__c object
        read from another set. After item 10 the two disposition personas have it; anyone holding
        ONLY this set does not, and their dashboard renders empty rather than erroring. Widening
        it is a decision, not a tidy up.
    -->
    <fieldPermissions>
        <editable>false</editable>
        <field>Property_Asset__c.Argus_Value__c</field>
        <readable>true</readable>
    </fieldPermissions>
    <fieldPermissions>
        <editable>false</editable>
        <field>Property_Asset__c.Readiness_Score__c</field>
        <readable>true</readable>
    </fieldPermissions>
    <fieldPermissions>
        <editable>false</editable>
        <field>Property_Asset__c.Property_Name__c</field>
        <readable>true</readable>
    </fieldPermissions>
    <fieldPermissions>
        <editable>true</editable>
        <field>Property_Asset__c.Property_Type__c</field>
        <readable>true</readable>
    </fieldPermissions>
    <fieldPermissions>
        <editable>false</editable>
        <field>Property_Asset__c.Sell_Readiness_Band__c</field>
        <readable>true</readable>
    </fieldPermissions>
    <fieldPermissions>
        <editable>true</editable>
        <field>Property_Asset__c.Sell_Readiness_Score__c</field>
        <readable>true</readable>
    </fieldPermissions>
    <hasActivationRequired>false</hasActivationRequired>
    <label>Disposition Dashboard Access</label>
</PermissionSet>
